IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg5-spectrum`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg5-licences`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg5-duties`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg5-schedules`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg5-radio`

-- THE 2001 TEXT.  The Regulations as made (S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001) are deposited and compared with the 2002 Revised Edition regulation by regulation in sgta-i-rg5-as-made.l4
-- (59 of the 80 regulations have the same words).  A function below that takes a date starts on 2 March 2001 where the regulation it encodes has the same words as made (regs 24, 57, 64, 65, 78),
-- differs only in the order of its paragraphs (reg 20), or did not yet exist (reg 65A: FALSE until S 461/2009); reg 76 answers with its as-made wording before 1 January 2003.
-- Functions of the other sibling modules that take no date answer on the Revised Edition's words; the comparison table says, regulation by regulation, whether those are the 2001 words.

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 5): the five amending instruments in IMDA's list,
-- each in its own section, with the commencement date as the date edge.  Texts: TA1999-RG5-S707-2005, -S263-2006, -S461-2009,
-- -S20-2011, -S100-2016 under subjects/sg/telecommunications-radio-communication-regulations-2001/registers/source-bundle/.
-- Each rule is the amended provision in its new form, answering NOTHING before the amending instrument's commencement.
-- Where a provision was amended in a way that changes what a person can be made to do, the older form is in the sibling module
-- named in the section heading (the form in the 2002 Revised Edition has no date guard of its own: its start date is not printed).
-- Amendments of Rg 5 regulation 65 and regulation 78 are in sgta-i-rg5-radio.l4.

§ `S 707/2005 (in operation 11 November 2005): regulation 16 substituted`

-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:15 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Radio-communication)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:16 | (Amendment) Regulations 2005 and shall come into operation on 11th November 2005.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:18 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 16
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:19 | 2. Regulation 16 of the Telecommunications (Radiocommunication) Regulations (Rg 5)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:20 | is deleted and the following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:21 | ‘‘Suspension or cancellation of spectrum right, etc.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:22 | 16.—(1) If the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:23 | (a) a person who is granted a spectrum right is contravening, or has
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:24 | contravened, whether by act or omission —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:25 | (i) any of the provisions of the Act or these Regulations; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:26 | (ii) any direction given to the person by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:27 | section 27, 32D or 32F (2) of the Act; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:28 | (b) a grant of the spectrum right was obtained by fraud or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:29 | misrepresentation,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:30 | the Authority may, by notice in writing and without payment of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:31 | compensation, suspend or cancel the grant of the spectrum right or part thereof.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:32 | (2) If the Authority is satisfied that a person who is granted a spectrum right is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:33 | contravening, or has contravened, whether by act or omission —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:34 | (a) any condition of the grant of the spectrum right; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:35 | (b) any direction given to the person by the Authority under section 5A (8)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:36 | of the Act,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:37 | the Authority may, by notice in writing and without payment of any
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:38 | compensation, do either or both of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:39 | (i) suspend or cancel the grant of the spectrum right or part thereof;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:40 | (ii) require the payment, within such time as may be specified, of a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:41 | financial penalty of such amount not exceeding $1 million as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:42 | Authority thinks fit.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:43 | (3) The Authority shall, before suspending or cancelling the grant of any spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:44 | right or part thereof under paragraph (1) or (2) (i) —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:45 | (a) give to the person to whom the spectrum right was granted notice in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:46 | writing of its intention to do so; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:47 | (b) in such notice call upon that person to show cause within such time as
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:48 | may be specified in the notice as to why his spectrum right or part thereof
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:49 | should not be suspended or cancelled.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:50 | (4) If the person to whom a notice has been given under paragraph (3) —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:51 | (a) fails to show cause within the period of time given to him to do so or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:52 | such extended period of time as the Authority may allow; or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:53 | (b) fails to show sufficient cause,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:54 | the Authority shall give notice in writing to that person of the date from which the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:55 | suspension or cancellation of his spectrum right or part thereof is to take effect.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:56 | (5) Any financial penalty payable by any person under paragraph (2) (ii) shall be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:57 | recoverable by the Authority as a debt due to the Authority from that person and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:58 | the person’s liability to pay shall not be affected by his spectrum right or any part
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:59 | thereof ceasing (for any reason) to be in force.’’.
@ref Rg 5 as amended by S 707/2005 (src:TA1999-RG5-S707-2005:15-59)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `a grant of the spectrum right was obtained by fraud or misrepresentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a provision of the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a direction of the Authority under section 27, 32D or 32F(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 16(1) (from 11 November 2005): the Authority may by written notice, without compensation, suspend or cancel the spectrum right or part of it` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (   `a grant of the spectrum right was obtained by fraud or misrepresentation`
                           OR `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a provision of the Act or these Regulations`
                           OR `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a direction of the Authority under section 27, 32D or 32F(2) of the Act`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a condition of the grant of the spectrum right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a direction of the Authority under section 5A(8) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 16(2) (from 11 November 2005): the Authority may by written notice suspend or cancel the spectrum right, or require a financial penalty, or both` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (   `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a condition of the grant of the spectrum right`
                           OR `the person contravenes, or has contravened, a direction of the Authority under section 5A(8) of the Act`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Authority gave the person written notice of its intention to suspend or cancel, calling on the person to show cause within a time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to show cause in time, or failed to show sufficient cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 16(3) and (4) (from 11 November 2005): the Authority may give notice of the date the suspension or cancellation takes effect` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the Authority gave the person written notice of its intention to suspend or cancel, calling on the person to show cause within a time` AND `the person failed to show cause in time, or failed to show sufficient cause`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 16(2)(ii) (S 707/2005 form, 11 November 2005 to 31 March 2016): the most the financial penalty may be, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 11 11 2005) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN JUST 1000000
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person's grant concerns a spectrum right the person holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 16(5) (from 11 November 2005): the penalty is a debt due to the Authority and the liability survives the spectrum right ceasing to be in force` MEANS
    (d AT LEAST (Date 11 11 2005)) AND `the person's grant concerns a spectrum right the person holds`

§ `S 263/2006 (in operation 1 June 2006; regulations 6 and 10 deemed in operation 1 May 2006)`

-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:14 | 1. —(1) These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:15 | communication) (Amendment) Regulations 2006 and shall, with the exception of regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:16 | 6 and 10, come into operation on 1st June 2006.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:17 | (2) Regulations 6 and 10 shall be deemed to have come into operation on 1st May 2006.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:19 | Amendment of regulation 19
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:20 | 2. Regulation 19 of the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Rg 5)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:21 | (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended by deleting
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:22 | paragraph (3) and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:23 | “(3) A licence shall be subject to such conditions, restrictions and limitations as the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:24 | Authority may determine and shall be valid —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:25 | (a) in the case of a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:26 | specified in regulation 25 (1) (b) or (c), for a period of 5 years; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:27 | (b) in any other case, for such period as the Authority may determine,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:28 | unless it is cancelled, suspended or reduced in duration in accordance with the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:29 | provisions of the Act or these Regulations.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:31 | Amendment of regulation 26
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:32 | 3. Regulation 26 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting paragraph (1) and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:33 | substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:34 | “(1) The licence fees payable for station licences and network licences are specified
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:36 | (a) in the case of a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence, in Part
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:37 | IA of the First Schedule; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:38 | (b) in any other case, in Part II of the First Schedule.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:40 | Amendment of regulation 30
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:41 | 4. The principal Regulations are amended by renumbering regulation 30 as paragraph (1) of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:42 | that regulation, and by inserting immediately thereafter the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:43 | “(2) It is a condition of every Ship Station Licence that the ship in respect of which
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:44 | the Ship Station Licence is granted remains registered or licensed in Singapore
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:45 | throughout the period of validity of the Ship Station Licence.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:46 | Amendment of regulation 34
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:47 | 5. The principal Regulations are amended by renumbering regulation 34 as paragraph (1) of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:48 | that regulation, and by inserting immediately thereafter the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:49 | “(2) It is a condition of every Aircraft Station Licence that the aircraft in respect of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:50 | which the Aircraft Station Licence is granted remains registered in Singapore
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:51 | throughout the period of validity of the Aircraft Station Licence.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:53 | Amendment of regulation 39
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:54 | 6. Regulation 39 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting paragraph (2) and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:55 | substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:56 | “(2) The fee payable to sit for the Radio Amateur Examination referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:57 | paragraph (1) (a) by —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:58 | (a) a full-time secondary, pre-university or tertiary student or a full-time
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:59 | student of the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, shall be $20; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:60 | (b) any other person, shall be $40.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:62 | New regulation 63A
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:63 | 7. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after regulation 63, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:64 | following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:65 | “Cancellation of Ship Station Licence or Aircraft Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:66 | 63A. —(1) The Authority may, by notice in writing, cancel —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:67 | (a) a Ship Station Licence granted in respect of a ship where the licensee has
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:68 | contravened the condition specified in regulation 30 (2); or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:69 | (b) an Aircraft Station Licence granted in respect of a station on an aircraft
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:70 | where the licensee has contravened the condition specified in regulation 34
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:71 | (2).
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:72 | (2) Where a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence is cancelled under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:73 | paragraph (1), no fee or part thereof shall be refunded by the Authority in respect of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:74 | the unexpired period of the licence.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:76 | Amendment of regulation 65
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:77 | 8. Regulation 65 (4) of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:78 | (a) by deleting the comma at the end of sub-paragraph (e) and substituting a semi-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:79 | colon, and by inserting immediately thereafter the following sub-paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:80 | “(f) a public wireless broadband access system,”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:81 | (b) by deleting the words “sub-paragraphs (a) to (e)” in the penultimate line and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:82 | substituting the words “sub-paragraphs (a) to (f)”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:84 | Amendment of First Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:85 | 9. The First Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:86 | (a) by inserting, immediately after Part I, the following Part:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:87 | “PART IA
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:88 | FEES FOR SHIP STATION LICENCE AND AIRCRAFT STATION LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:90 | First column Second column
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:91 | Types of licences Fees payable
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:92 | 1. Ship Station $100 for 5 years
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:93 | 2. Aircraft Station $100 for 5 years.”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:95 | (b) by deleting the heading in Part II and substituting the following heading:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:97 | “FEES FOR STATION LICENCE AND NETWORK LICENCE (OTHER THAN SHIP
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:98 | STATION LICENCE AND AIRCRAFT STATION LICENCE)”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:100 | (c) by deleting items 1 and 2 in Part II.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:102 | Deletion of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:103 | 10. The Second Schedule to the principal Regulations is deleted.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:104 | [G.N. No. S 707/2005]
@ref Rg 5 as amended by S 263/2006 (src:TA1999-RG5-S263-2006:14-104)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licence is a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence specified in regulation 25(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of years the Authority determined` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 19(3) (from 1 June 2006): the licence is valid for this many years unless cancelled, suspended or reduced` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the licence is a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence specified in regulation 25(1)(b) or (c)` THEN JUST 5
           OTHERWISE JUST `the number of years the Authority determined`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licence is a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 5 reg 26(1) (from 1 June 2006): the Part of the First Schedule that specifies the licence fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the licence is a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence` THEN JUST "Part IA"
           OTHERWISE JUST "Part II"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the ship remains registered or licensed in Singapore throughout the period of validity of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 30(2) (from 1 June 2006): the condition of the Ship Station Licence is met` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the ship remains registered or licensed in Singapore throughout the period of validity of the licence`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the aircraft remains registered in Singapore throughout the period of validity of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 34(2) (from 1 June 2006): the condition of the Aircraft Station Licence is met` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the aircraft remains registered in Singapore throughout the period of validity of the licence`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the examinee is a full-time secondary, pre-university or tertiary student, or a full-time student of the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 39(2) (deemed in operation from 1 May 2006): the fee to sit the Radio Amateur Examination in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2006) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the examinee is a full-time secondary, pre-university or tertiary student, or a full-time student of the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore` THEN JUST 20
           OTHERWISE JUST 40

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Second Schedule: the Schedule is in force on the date (deleted from 1 May 2006)` MEANS
    d LESS THAN (Date 1 5 2006)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee contravened the condition in regulation 30(2) (ship) or 34(2) (aircraft)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 63A(1) (from 1 June 2006): the Authority may by written notice cancel the Ship Station Licence or Aircraft Station Licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licensee contravened the condition in regulation 30(2) (ship) or 34(2) (aircraft)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 63A(2) (from 1 June 2006): the Authority refunds any part of the fee for the unexpired period of a licence cancelled under reg 63A(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licence is a Ship Station Licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `A fee for a period`
`Rg 5 First Schedule Part IA (from 1 June 2006): the fee for a Ship Station Licence or an Aircraft Station Licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2006) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`A fee for a period` OF 100, 5)

§ `S 461/2009 (in operation 2 October 2009)`

-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:16 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Radio-communication)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:17 | (Amendment) Regulations 2009 and shall come into operation on 2nd October 2009.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:19 | Amendment of regulation 2
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:20 | 2. Regulation 2 of the Telecommunications (Radio-communication) Regulations (Rg 5)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:21 | (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:22 | (a) by deleting the definition of “class licence” and substituting the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:23 | definition:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:24 | “ “class licence” means an individual station class licence referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:25 | regulation 65 or a station (spectrum) class licence referred to in regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:26 | 65A;”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:27 | (b) by inserting, immediately after the definition of “class licensee”, the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:28 | definitions:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:29 | “ “individual station class licence” means an individual station class licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:30 | referred to in regulation 65;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:31 | “individual station class licensee” means a person who is deemed to have
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:32 | been granted an individual station class licence;”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:33 | (c) by inserting, immediately after the definition of “station licence”, the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:34 | definitions:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:35 | “ “station (spectrum) class licence” means a station (spectrum) class licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:36 | referred to in regulation 65A;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:37 | “station (spectrum) class licensee” means a person who is deemed to have
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:38 | been granted a station (spectrum) class licence;”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:40 | Amendment of regulation 23
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:41 | 3. Regulation 23 of the principal Regulations is amended by inserting, immediately after
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:42 | paragraph (3), the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:43 | “(4) In this regulation and regulation 24, “station” does not include a radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:44 | communication station specified in the Fourth Schedule.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:45 | Deletion and substitution of heading to Part VIII
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:46 | 4. The heading to Part VIII of the principal Regulations is deleted and the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:47 | heading substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:49 | “INDIVIDUAL STATION CLASS LICENCE AND STATION (SPECTRUM)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:50 | CLASS LICENCE”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:52 | Amendment of regulation 65
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:53 | 5. Regulation 65 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:54 | (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “A person” in paragraph (1), the words “,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:55 | other than a telecommunication licensee,”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:56 | (b) by deleting the words “a class licence” in paragraphs (1) and (3) and substituting in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:57 | each case the words “an individual station class licence”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:58 | (c) by deleting the words “A class licence” in paragraph (2) and substituting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:59 | “An individual station class licence”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:60 | (d) by deleting the regulation heading and substituting the following regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:61 | heading:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:63 | “Grant of individual station class licences”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:65 | New regulation 65A
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:66 | 6. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after regulation 65, the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:67 | following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:69 | “Grant of station (spectrum) class licences
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:70 | 65A.—(1) A telecommunication licensee who operates a radio-communication station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:71 | specified in the Fourth Schedule shall be deemed to have been granted a station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:72 | (spectrum) class licence by the Authority for that purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:73 | (2) A station (spectrum) class licence shall be subject to the conditions specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:74 | Fifth Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:75 | (3) No fee is payable for the grant of a station (spectrum) class licence.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:77 | Amendment of Third Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:78 | 7. The Third Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:79 | (a) by deleting the words “A class licensee” in paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 and substituting
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:80 | in each case the words “An individual station class licensee”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:81 | (b) by deleting the words “a class licence” in paragraph 4 and substituting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:82 | “an individual station class licence”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:83 | (c) by deleting the words “class licensee” in paragraph 4 and substituting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:84 | “individual station class licensee”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:85 | (d) by deleting the words “CLASS LICENCE” in the Schedule heading and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:86 | substituting the words “INDIVIDUAL STATION CLASS LICENCE”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:87 | New Fourth and Fifth Schedules
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:88 | 8. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after the Third
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:89 | Schedule, the following Schedules:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:91 | “FOURTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:93 | Regulations 23(4) and 65A(1)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:95 | RADIO-COMMUNICATION STATION OPERATED BY TELECOMMUNICATION
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:96 | LICENSEE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:97 | 1. A femtocell with an output power limit that does not exceed 100 mW EIRP and which is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:98 | connected to a telecommunication licensee’s public cellular mobile telephone system or
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:99 | public wireless broadband access system.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:101 | FIFTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:103 | Regulation 65A(2)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:105 | CONDITIONS OF STATION (SPECTRUM) CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:106 | 1. A station (spectrum) class licensee shall comply with the technical specifications laid
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:107 | down from time to time by the Authority in relation to the radio-communication station.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:108 | 2. A station (spectrum) class licensee shall ensure that the radio-communication station is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:109 | approved by the Authority before it is used for connection to any telecommunication system
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:110 | or equipment belonging to a public telecommunication licensee, and that the radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:111 | communication station is not tampered with or, without just cause, modified in any manner
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:112 | after the approval of the Authority has been obtained.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:113 | 3. A station (spectrum) class licensee shall, at its own cost and as required by the Authority,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:114 | conduct inspections of the radio-communication station in order to satisfy the Authority that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:115 | the radio-communication station has not been tampered with or, without just cause, modified
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:116 | in any manner after the approval of the Authority has been obtained.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:117 | 4. A station (spectrum) class licensee shall ensure that the radio-communication station is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:118 | not used for any unlawful purpose.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:119 | 5. The Authority may cancel or suspend a station (spectrum) class licence if it is satisfied
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:120 | that the station (spectrum) class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:121 | again to contravene, any of these conditions or the provisions of the Act.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:122 | 6. A station (spectrum) class licensee shall ensure that the radio-communication station
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:123 | operates only within the radio frequency spectrum assigned to the station (spectrum) class
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:124 | licensee.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:125 | 7. A station (spectrum) class licensee shall keep up-to-date records of the radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:126 | communication station, including details of the installation location of the radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:127 | communication station, the name of the equipment manufacturer, the model and serial
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:128 | number of the equipment, and the frequency, output power, date of purchase and date of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:129 | disposal of the equipment, and shall submit such records to the Authority as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:130 | may, from time to time, require.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:131 | Miscellaneous amendments
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:132 | 9. The principal Regulations are amended by deleting the words “or a network (spectrum)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:133 | licence” in the following provisions and substituting in each case the words “, a network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:134 | (spectrum) licence or a station (spectrum) class licence”:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:135 | Regulations 10(d), 11(2) and 12(1).
@ref Rg 5 as amended by S 461/2009 (src:TA1999-RG5-S461-2009:16-135)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `it is an individual station class licence referred to in regulation 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a station (spectrum) class licence referred to in regulation 65A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 2 (from 2 October 2009): the licence is a "class licence"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`it is an individual station class licence referred to in regulation 65` OR `it is a station (spectrum) class licence referred to in regulation 65A`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `it is a radio-communication station specified in the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 23(4) (from 2 October 2009): "station" in regulations 23 and 24 includes this radio-communication station` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `it is a radio-communication station specified in the Fourth Schedule`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `it is a femtocell` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its output power limit in milliwatts EIRP` IS A NUMBER
      `it is connected to a telecommunication licensee's public cellular mobile telephone system or public wireless broadband access system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Fourth Schedule item 1 (from 2 October 2009): this is a radio-communication station operated by a telecommunication licensee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`it is a femtocell` AND (`its output power limit in milliwatts EIRP` AT MOST 100) AND `it is connected to a telecommunication licensee's public cellular mobile telephone system or public wireless broadband access system`)

GIVEN `complies with the technical specifications the Authority laid down` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by the Authority before connection to a public telecommunication licensee's system or equipment, and not tampered with or, without just cause, modified afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conducts, at its own cost and as the Authority requires, inspections to satisfy the Authority the station has not been tampered with or modified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station is not used for any unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the station operates only within the radio frequency spectrum assigned to the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee keeps up-to-date records of the station (location, manufacturer, model and serial number, frequency, output power, date of purchase and of disposal) and submits them as required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Fifth Schedule items 1 to 4, 6 and 7: the station (spectrum) class licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
        `complies with the technical specifications the Authority laid down`
    AND `approved by the Authority before connection to a public telecommunication licensee's system or equipment, and not tampered with or, without just cause, modified afterwards`
    AND `conducts, at its own cost and as the Authority requires, inspections to satisfy the Authority the station has not been tampered with or modified`
    AND `the station is not used for any unlawful purpose`
    AND `the station operates only within the radio frequency spectrum assigned to the licensee`
    AND `the licensee keeps up-to-date records of the station (location, manufacturer, model and serial number, frequency, output power, date of purchase and of disposal) and submits them as required`

GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the station (spectrum) class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, these conditions or the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Fifth Schedule item 5: the Authority may cancel or suspend the station (spectrum) class licence` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied the station (spectrum) class licensee is contravening, or has contravened and is likely again to contravene, these conditions or the provisions of the Act`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Third Schedule conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 Third Schedule (from 2 October 2009): the individual station class licensee is meeting the conditions of the individual station class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the Third Schedule conditions are met`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person has, and complies with the conditions of, a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence or a station (spectrum) class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority permitted the operation without one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 11(2) (from 2 October 2009): the person is authorised to operate the station or network` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 10 2009) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the person has, and complies with the conditions of, a station (spectrum) licence, a network (spectrum) licence or a station (spectrum) class licence` OR `the Authority permitted the operation without one`)

§ `S 20/2011 (in operation 21 January 2011)`

-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:23 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:24 | (Radio-communication) (Amendment) Regulations 2011 and shall
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:25 | come into operation on 21st January 2011.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:27 | Amendment of regulation 76
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:28 | 2. Regulation 76 of the Telecommunications (Radio-
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:29 | communication) Regulations (Rg 5) is amended by deleting the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:30 | words ‘‘the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:31 | Telecommunication Services 2000 (G.N. No. S 412/2000) issued by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:32 | the Authority under section 26 of the Act’’ and substituting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:33 | ‘‘the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:34 | Telecommunication Services issued by the Authority under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:35 | section 26(1) of the Act, as may be amended from time to time’’.
@ref Rg 5 as amended by S 20/2011 (src:TA1999-RG5-S20-2011:23-35)
-- Regulation 76 as made (S 114/2001, in operation 2 March 2001) names the Code without the words "2000 (G.N. No. S 412/2000)", which the 2002 Revised Edition's text adds:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1518 | Application of Telecom Competition Code
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1519 | 76. No approval, consent, licence or authorisation given by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1520 | Authority pursuant to these Regulations shall be taken as specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1521 | authorising or approving any act or thing for the purposes of the Code
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1522 | of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1523 | Services issued by the Authority under section 26 of the Act.
@ref Rg 5 reg 76 as made (src:TA1999-RG5-S114-2001:1518-1523)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 5 reg 76: the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication Services that the regulation refers to` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 1 2003) THEN JUST "the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication Services issued by the Authority under section 26 of the Act"
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 1 2011) THEN JUST "the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication Services 2000 (G.N. No. S 412/2000) issued by the Authority under section 26 of the Act"
           OTHERWISE JUST "the Code of Practice for Competition in the provision of Telecommunication Services issued by the Authority under section 26(1) of the Act, as may be amended from time to time"

§ `S 100/2016 (in operation 1 April 2016)`

-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:26 | 2. Regulation 6 of the Telecommunications (Radio-communication)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:27 | Regulations (Rg 5) (called in these Regulations the principal
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:28 | Regulations) is amended by inserting, immediately after paragraph
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:29 | (2), the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:30 | “(3) A person specified in section 4(b) of the Act who is
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:31 | granted a spectrum right under section 5A of the Act must,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:32 | instead of the charges under paragraph (2), pay the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:33 | fees for the grant of a right to use any specified part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:34 | radio frequency spectrum referred to in paragraph (1):
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:35 | (a) application and processing fees as specified in Part III
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:36 | of the First Schedule;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:37 | (b) annual fees as specified in Part IV of the First
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:38 | Schedule.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:40 | Amendment of regulation 10
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:41 | 3. Regulation 10 of the principal Regulations is amended ––
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:42 | (a) by deleting the words “paragraph (f)” in paragraph (g) and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:43 | substituting the words “sub-paragraph (f)”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:44 | S 100/2016 2
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:46 | (b) by inserting, immediately after the words “determined
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:47 | by the Authority” in paragraph (h), the words “under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:48 | regulation 6(2)”;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:49 | (c) by deleting the word “or” at the end of paragraph (i), and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:50 | by inserting immediately thereafter the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:51 | “(ia) conditions requiring the person granted the spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:52 | right (called the first person) to share, in accordance
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:53 | with a written notice from the Authority, all or part
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:54 | of the radio frequency spectrum allocated to the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:55 | first person with the person specified in the notice
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:56 | (called the second person) for the second person’s
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:57 | use during a national event or where such use is in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:58 | the public interest; or”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:59 | (d) by renumbering the regulation as paragraph (1) of that
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:60 | regulation, and by inserting immediately thereafter the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:61 | following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:62 | “(2) The written notice referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:63 | paragraph (1)(ia) ––
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:64 | (a) must specify the period (not exceeding 90 days
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:65 | at a time) during which the Authority requires
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:66 | the first person to share the radio frequency
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:67 | spectrum with the second person; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:68 | (b) may include any direction of the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:69 | under section 5A(8) of the Act to the first
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:70 | person to take such measures specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:71 | written notice to facilitate the sharing of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:72 | radio frequency spectrum.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:74 | Amendment of regulation 12
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:75 | 4. Regulation 12(1) of the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:76 | deleting the words “Subject to such conditions as the Authority may
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:77 | generally or specifically impose, a person granted a spectrum right
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:78 | may” and substituting the words “A person granted a spectrum
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:79 | right may, with the Authority’s prior written approval and subject
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:80 | to such conditions as the Authority may generally or specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:81 | impose,”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:82 | 3 S 100/2016
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:84 | Amendment of regulation 16
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:85 | 5. Regulation 16(2) of the principal Regulations is amended
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:86 | by deleting sub-paragraph (ii) and substituting the following
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:87 | sub‑paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:88 | “(ii) require the person to pay, within such time as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:89 | specified in the notice, a financial penalty of an amount
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:90 | not exceeding the higher of the following amounts:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:91 | (A) 10% of the annual turnover of that part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:92 | person’s business in respect of which the person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:93 | is granted the spectrum right, as ascertained
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:94 | from the person’s latest audited accounts;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:95 | (B) $1 million.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:97 | Amendment of regulation 20
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:98 | 6. Regulation 20 of the principal Regulations is amended
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:99 | by deleting the words “Business Registration Act (Cap. 32)”
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:100 | in paragraph (b) and substituting the words “Business Names
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:101 | Registration Act 2014 (Act 29 of 2014)”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:103 | Amendment of regulation 24
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:104 | 7. Regulation 24 of the principal Regulations is amended ––
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:105 | (a) by deleting paragraphs (2), (3) and (4); and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:106 | (b) by deleting the words “and records” in the regulation heading.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:108 | Amendment of regulation 25
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:109 | 8. Regulation 25 of the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:110 | inserting, immediately after paragraph (2), the following paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:111 | “(2A) It is a condition of every station licence and network
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:112 | licence that the licensee must comply with any direction by the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:113 | Authority specified in a written notice to share all or part of the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:114 | radio frequency band (allocated to the licensee) with another
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:115 | person specified in the notice for that other person’s use during
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:116 | a national event or where such use is in the public interest.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:117 | (2B) The written notice referred to in paragraph (2A) ––
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:118 | (a) must specify the period (not exceeding 90 days at a time)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:119 | during which the Authority requires the licensee to share
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:120 | the radio frequency band with the other person; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:121 | S 100/2016 4
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:123 | (b) may include any direction of the Authority to the licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:124 | to take such measures specified in the written notice to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:125 | facilitate the sharing of the radio frequency band.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:127 | Amendment of regulation 29
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:128 | 9. Regulation 29 of the principal Regulations is amended ––
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:129 | (a) by deleting sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of paragraph (1)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:130 | and substituting the following sub-paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:131 | “(a) the ship on which the station is to be carried has a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:132 | valid Ship Registry Certificate issued by the Maritime
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:133 | and Port Authority of Singapore (established under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:134 | section 4 of the Maritime and Port Authority of
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:135 | Singapore Act (Cap. 170A));
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:136 | (b) the person applying for the Ship Station Licence
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:137 | furnishes the documents and information required
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:138 | by the Authority for the purpose of the application;
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:139 | and”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:140 | (b) by deleting the words “required by the Authority in the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:141 | application form” in paragraph (2) and substituting the
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:142 | words “and documents required by the Authority in respect
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:143 | of the application form”.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:145 | Deletion of regulation 57
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:146 | 10. Regulation 57 of the principal Regulations is deleted.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:148 | Deletion of regulation 64
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:149 | 11. Regulation 64 of the principal Regulations is deleted.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:151 | Amendment of regulation 75
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:152 | 12. Regulation 75 of the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:153 | inserting, immediately after paragraph (2), the following paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:154 | “(3) Despite paragraph (2), a permit may be granted under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:155 | paragraph (1) for the use of a radio frequency band referred
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:156 | to in paragraph (2) during a national event or where such use
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:157 | is in the public interest.
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:158 | (4) Where ––
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:159 | (a) the Authority has granted a permit under paragraph (1)
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:160 | to a person (called the first person) to use a radio
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:161 | frequency band; and
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:162 | 5 S 100/2016
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:164 | (b) the Authority subsequently grants another permit under
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:165 | paragraph (1) to a person (called the second person) to
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:166 | use all or part of that radio frequency band during a
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:167 | national event or where such use is in the public interest,
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:168 | the Authority may, by a written notice, require the first person
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:169 | to share all or part of that radio frequency band for such period
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:170 | specified in the written notice and take such measures specified
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:171 | in the written notice to facilitate the second person’s use of all
-- src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:172 | or part of that radio frequency band.”.
@ref Rg 5 as amended by S 100/2016 (src:TA1999-RG5-S100-2016:26-172)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person is specified in section 4(b) of the Act and is granted a spectrum right under section 5A of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 6(3) (from 1 April 2016): the person pays the Part III and Part IV fees instead of the charges under regulation 6(2)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the person is specified in section 4(b) of the Act and is granted a spectrum right under section 5A of the Act`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the written notice specifies the period (not exceeding 90 days at a time) during which the first person must share the spectrum with the second person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 10(1)(ia) and (2) (from 1 April 2016): the written notice requiring the first person to share the spectrum is valid` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the written notice specifies the period (not exceeding 90 days at a time) during which the first person must share the spectrum with the second person`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Authority gave its prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is within the conditions the Authority imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 12(1) (from 1 April 2016): the person granted a spectrum right may authorise another person to use the assigned spectrum` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the Authority gave its prior written approval` AND `the authorisation is within the conditions the Authority imposed`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act (before 1 April 2016) or the Business Names Registration Act 2014 (from 1 April 2016)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 20(b): the Authority may grant a licence other than a class licence to this registered business` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the person is a business registered under the Business Registration Act (before 1 April 2016) or the Business Names Registration Act 2014 (from 1 April 2016)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 24(2) to (4): the licensee must keep and submit records of the equipment, and permit inspection of them` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee complies with a direction in the written notice to share all or part of the radio frequency band with another person for a national event or in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the period (not exceeding 90 days at a time)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 25(2A) and (2B) (from 1 April 2016): the station licence or network licence condition on sharing is met` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the licensee complies with a direction in the written notice to share all or part of the radio frequency band with another person for a national event or in the public interest` AND `the notice specifies the period (not exceeding 90 days at a time)`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the ship has a valid Ship Registry Certificate issued by the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant furnishes the documents and information the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship complies with the other requirements the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 29(1) (from 1 April 2016): the Ship Station Licence may be granted` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the ship has a valid Ship Registry Certificate issued by the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore` AND `the applicant furnishes the documents and information the Authority requires` AND `the ship complies with the other requirements the Authority determined`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 57 and reg 64: the duty on a network licensee to keep records (reg 57), and on a licensee to notify a change of particulars within 14 days (reg 64), is in force on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 2 3 2001) THEN NOTHING
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the permit is granted for use of a band that is within a spectrum right or licence, during a national event or in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 75(3) (from 1 April 2016): a permit may be granted under regulation 75(1) despite regulation 75(2)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the permit is granted for use of a band that is within a spectrum right or licence, during a national event or in the public interest`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Authority granted a permit to the first person and then another permit to the second person for all or part of the band during a national event or in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 5 reg 75(4) (from 1 April 2016): the Authority may by written notice require the first person to share the band and take measures` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the Authority granted a permit to the first person and then another permit to the second person for all or part of the band during a national event or in the public interest`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `annual turnover of that part of the person's business in respect of which the spectrum right was granted, from the latest audited accounts, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 16(2)(ii) (S 100/2016 form, from 1 April 2016): the most the financial penalty may be, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN NOTHING
           IF (`annual turnover of that part of the person's business in respect of which the spectrum right was granted, from the latest audited accounts, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 10) GREATER THAN 1000000
              THEN JUST (`annual turnover of that part of the person's business in respect of which the spectrum right was granted, from the latest audited accounts, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 10)
           OTHERWISE JUST 1000000

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `annual turnover of that part of the person's business in respect of which the spectrum right was granted, from the latest audited accounts, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 5 reg 16(2)(ii): the most the financial penalty may be, in dollars, on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2016) THEN `Rg 5 reg 16(2)(ii) (S 707/2005 form, 11 November 2005 to 31 March 2016): the most the financial penalty may be, in dollars` d
           OTHERWISE `Rg 5 reg 16(2)(ii) (S 100/2016 form, from 1 April 2016): the most the financial penalty may be, in dollars` d `annual turnover of that part of the person's business in respect of which the spectrum right was granted, from the latest audited accounts, in dollars`

